  lines:
  - Text
  - Button
  - You completed the game, thank you for playing
  - Dialogue
  - Moving
  - Puzzle
  - You are now in dialogue mode. When you switch modes, the game will tell you which
    mode you're in by saying either Text, if there is text on the screen or Moving,
    if you can move. When the game is waiting for your input, you'll hear this sound.
    Press X, the bottom of the four buttons on the right side of your controller,
    to continue.
  - doors remaining
  - 0
  - 1
  - 2
  - 4
  - 5
  - 6
  - 7
  - 8
  - 9
  - Try to press the four buttons on the right side of your controller while the
    music plays. The more intervals you unlock, the more you can play
  - Solution interval
  - First
  - Second
  - Third
  - Fourth
  - Score
  - Input
  - Same note, prime
  - Medium distance, fifth
  - Big distance, octave
  - Cutscene
  - On your right side in the back you have two buttons. Press the one in the front
    to interact
  - You are now in a room with an exit. Find the door you can interact with, then
    press the right button.
  - Hello?
  - Is anyone there?
  - Oh thank goodness, you are moving. Are you hurt?
  - "Easy, easy. I\u2019ll help you get up."
  - "It is so dark in here, glad I didn\u2019t stumble over you."
  - Aaaaand no one else around, just the two of us for now.
  - Your friend's out there somewhere, I just know it. Same with the rest of my band.
  - Come on, I've got your back. Let's move.
  - Wait, you actually got it open?!
  - Okay, that... actually feels really good. Makes me want to play something.
  - Go on, try it. Use what you just learned! Just sing along with us
  - Helloooo?! Anyone?!
  - Oh, Henry! And... a new face, hi! Okay good, more people, less scary.
  - Check it out, the tour guide gave me this thing. It's supposed to vibrate when
    we're headed toward the exit.
  - Except it just vibrates whenever it feels like it. Super helpful, thanks.
  - Here, you take it. Maybe you can figure out how it works. I'm tagging along!
  - Ooh, a music puzzle! Now THIS I know about. You look a little lost, let me break
    it down!
  - So, an interval is just the distance between two notes.
  - Depending on how far apart those notes are, the interval gets a different name.
  - Smallest distance? That's called the prime.
  - Literally the same note played twice, so the gap is basically nothing.
  - Now the opposite. The biggest gap is the octave.
  - The two notes way far apart, like... if the first note was on your feet, the
    second would be all the way at your head.
  - Okay so, there's a sequence of intervals here, but where do we even type it in?
  - Okay so, where's the actual solution? The door wants a sequence, but I don't
    see the solution anywhere.
  - Well, look who it is! About time, I was starting to think I'd have to solve this
    whole labyrinth myself.
  - Found this door ages ago. It just won't open. I am going insane.
  - It wants a sequence of intervals. I know the fifth, that one's easy.
  - Medium gap between the two notes. Listen, it sounds like this!
  - Alright, your turn. Don't mess this up, we're a team now.
  - HA! I never doubted you!
  - And now I've picked up the prime and the octave too. Give me five minutes with
    those and play along!
